<!-- Final Stabilization (§6): overflow/more affordance for the compact
     transfer-management control. Simple three-dot vertical, matching the
     stroke style of the app's other 24dp glyphs.
     Post-v1.0 legibility pass: dot radius 1.9 -> 2.15 (the glyph's ink
     coverage was small enough that at 16-18dp it read as faint specks
     even with a visible tint) — still unmistakably the Material
     more_vert glyph, just legible at row scale.
     Post-v1.0 pass 2 (§unmissable-overflow): 2.15 -> 2.4 with a hairline
     of extra vertical spread (4.85 -> 4.7 start). The user reported the
     affordance "clickable but invisible" against the shipped build — the
     true killer there was the mask-only ripple outline erasure (fixed in
     bg_icon_ripple.xml), and this bolder glyph ensures it can never read
     as faint again on any panel.
     Pass-14 (per direct feedback "more minimalist and less bold — its
     current appearance is too heavy"): with the ripple-erasure bug long
     fixed, the 2.4-radius + brightest-tint combination now overcorrects
     into a heavy blob at row scale. Dots back to a refined 1.8 radius
     with the original 4.85 vertical spread — the classic Material
     more_vert proportion — and DeviceAdapter renders it 16dp at
     text_secondary instead of 18dp at text_primary, so the affordance
     reads as quiet chrome rather than a fourth headline. Still on the
     full 32dp touch target, so it stays perfectly tappable. -->
